Package: recombClust
Type: Package
Title: Group Chromosomes by Their Recombination History
Version: 2.0.0
Date: 2026-07-12
Authors@R: c(
    person("Carlos", "Ruiz-Arenas", email = "carlos.ruiz@isglobal.org", role = "aut"),
    person("Dolors", "Pelegri-Siso", email = "dolors.pelegri@isglobal.org",
           role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-5993-3003")),
    person("Alejandro", "Caceres", email = "alejandro.caceres@isglobal.org", role = "aut"),
    person("Juan R.", "Gonzalez", email = "juanr.gonzalez@isglobal.org",
           role = "aut", comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-3267-2146")))
Description: Infers the recombination history of chromosomes from phased genotypes.
    A mixture model classifies, for each pair of SNP-blocks, chromosomes into a
    linked (low-recombination) and a recombined population; aggregating many pairs
    over a region groups the chromosomes into sub-populations with different
    recombination histories -- for example the two orientations of a chromosomal
    inversion -- and locates the region responsible. From version 2.0.0 the
    computational core runs in C++ on HDF5 files through the BigDataStatMeth API, so
    the analysis scales out-of-core to large cohorts. Method: Ruiz-Arenas et al.
    (2020) <doi:10.1101/gr.258301.119>.
Depends: R (>= 3.6.0), BigDataStatMeth
